    "text": "To determine the total amount of money Meghan had, we need to calculate the value of each type of bill separately and then sum these values.\n\n1. Calculate the value of the $100 bills:\n   Meghan has 2 $100 bills.\n   \\[\n   2 \\times 100 = 200\n   \\]\n   So, the $100 bills are worth $200.\n\n2. Calculate the value of the $50 bills:\n   Meghan has 5 $50 bills.\n   \\[\n   5 \\times 50 = 250\n   \\]\n   So, the $50 bills are worth $250.\n\n3. Calculate the value of the $10 bills:\n   Meghan has 10 $10 bills.\n   \\[\n   10 \\times 10 = 100\n   \\]\n   So, the $10 bills are worth $100.\n\n4. Sum the values of all the bills to find the total amount of money:\n   \\[\n   200 + 250 + 100 = 550\n   \\]\n   Therefore, the total amount of money Meghan had is \\(\\boxed{550}\\).",
